('128.5.b.8.A',4,'The topic of a story is one word, like friendship. Which sentence states a theme?','["Pets", "True friends help each other in hard times.", "A park", "Jumping rope"]'::jsonb,1,'A theme is a full-sentence message about life.','original'),
('128.5.b.8.B',3,'A major character differs from a minor character because the major character:','["has no name", "never speaks", "is more central to the plot", "appears only once"]'::jsonb,2,'Major characters drive the story.','original'),
('128.5.b.8.B',3,'A sidekick who helps the hero now and then is usually a:','["narrator", "theme", "setting", "minor character"]'::jsonb,3,'Minor characters support the main characters.','original'),
('128.5.b.8.C',3,'The order in which events happen in a story is its:','["sequence", "caption", "glossary", "rhyme"]'::jsonb,0,'Plot elements include the sequence of events.','original'),
('128.5.b.8.C',3,'The part that solves the main problem is the:','["setting", "resolution", "dialogue", "exposition"]'::jsonb,1,'The resolution ends the conflict.','original'),
('128.5.b.8.D',3,'A story set during a flood makes the characters:','["ignore the weather", "stay unchanged", "face dangers that shape the plot", "forget the plot"]'::jsonb,2,'Setting influences events.','original'),
