('128.5.b.9.A',3,'A fable is a short story that:','["teaches a lesson, often with talking animals", "tells a real person''s life", "lists facts in a table", "gives step-by-step directions"]'::jsonb,0,'Fables teach morals.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.A',3,'Which is a feature of a fairy tale?','["a glossary", "magic and a happily-ever-after ending", "a timeline", "a recipe"]'::jsonb,1,'Fairy tales include magic and set endings.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.B',3,'In a poem, lines that end with the same sound have:','["captions", "dialogue", "rhyme", "a glossary"]'::jsonb,2,'Rhyme is a sound device.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.B',3,'In a poem with rhyme scheme ABAB, lines 1 and 3:','["never rhyme", "are the same word", "are in different stanzas", "rhyme with each other"]'::jsonb,3,'Matching letters show matching end sounds.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.C',3,'The main divisions of a play are called:','["acts", "stanzas", "chapters", "captions"]'::jsonb,0,'Plays are divided into acts.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.C',3,'In a play, stage directions tell actors:','["the price", "how to move or speak", "the page number", "the author''s age"]'::jsonb,1,'Directions guide performance.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.D.i',3,'To find the central idea of an informational text, ask:','["Who printed it?", "How many words are bold?", "What is this text mostly about?", "Where is the index?"]'::jsonb,2,'The central idea is the main point.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.D.i',3,'Which detail supports the central idea ''Recycling helps the planet''?','["Trees are tall.", "Paper is white.", "Bins are blue.", "Recycling paper saves trees."]'::jsonb,3,'Supporting evidence connects to the central idea.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.D.ii',2,'Bold words in a text usually show:','["important terms", "the author''s name", "mistakes", "jokes"]'::jsonb,0,'Print features highlight key words.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.D.ii',3,'A table in an informational text is used to:','["show a rhyme", "organize facts in rows and columns", "tell a joke", "list the author''s pets"]'::jsonb,1,'Tables organize data.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.D.iii',3,'Which words signal cause and effect?','["above, below, beside", "first, next, then", "because, so, as a result", "however, but, although"]'::jsonb,2,'Cause and effect uses signal words like because and as a result.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.D.iii',3,'A text explains a problem and then ways to fix it. Its organizational pattern is:','["compare and contrast", "sequence", "description", "problem and solution"]'::jsonb,3,'Problem and solution shows a problem and its answers.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.E.i',3,'Which sentence states a claim?','["Schools should start later in the morning.", "Schools have classrooms.", "Some buses are yellow.", "The bell rang at eight."]'::jsonb,0,'A claim is an arguable position.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.E.ii',3,'Which sentence about the ocean is an opinion?','["Whales live in the ocean.", "The ocean is the prettiest place to visit.", "The ocean has salt water.", "The ocean covers most of Earth."]'::jsonb,1,'Opinions state beliefs and cannot be proved.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.E.ii',3,'Which statement about the sun is a fact?','["The sun is the nicest star.", "Sunny days are the best days.", "The sun is a star.", "Everyone loves hot weather."]'::jsonb,2,'Facts can be proved.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.E.iii',3,'A text with simple words and bright pictures about letters is likely meant for:','["lawyers", "pilots", "scientists", "young children"]'::jsonb,3,'Intended audience shapes language and design.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.E.iii',3,'An author who uses technical terms in a report about engines is writing for:','["readers who know the topic", "babies", "pets", "no one"]'::jsonb,0,'Technical language suggests an informed audience.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.F',2,'A website with videos, links and sound is a:','["printed poem", "digital and multimodal text", "paper map only", "handwritten letter"]'::jsonb,1,'Digital texts can combine modes.','original'),
('128.5.b.9.F',3,'A multimodal text combines:','["only numbers", "only blank space", "words with images, sound or video", "only words"]'::jsonb,2,'Multimodal means more than one mode.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
